.TH CCHAN_MSG_COUNT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cchan_msg_count \- get the current message count of a direction
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

size_t cchan_msg_count(cchan *ch, cchan_direction d);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns how many messages the queue of the given direction holds at
the moment of the call.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
ch   Channel to ask
d    Direction to ask about (cchan_owner_to_workers or
     cchan_workers_to_owner)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
The number of messages in that direction, or (size_t)-1 when the
cchan is NULL or the direction is not valid.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Reading the count is thread-safe, but it is only a snapshot: other
threads can change it as soon as the call returns.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cchan_send (3),
.BR cchan_recv (3)
